<speak>Good. I have a bad habit of reading a message on the telephone and thinking I will deal with it later on the computer. Then, because I have already opened it, it no longer catches my attention. A clear subject line helps me find it again. I am not asking for more messages, just ones I can recognise. My business inbox is full of headings like 'urgent update' which turn out to be nothing urgent at all. For personal matters, plain language is much better. Tell me it is about scheduling or correspondence, and I know where it belongs in my little system.</speak>